1
00:00:00,040 --> 00:00:07,361
Let's learn English on a hike.
一起边徒步边学英语吧。

2
00:00:07,361 --> 00:00:14,041
So I guess I should start this lesson by explaining the difference between going for a walk and going for a hike.
我想先从散步和徒步的区别讲起。

3
00:00:14,041 --> 00:00:19,441
When you go for a walk it usually means that you are in the city or you are in town.
说去散步，通常指在城市或镇上走走。

4
00:00:19,441 --> 00:00:25,481
You go for a walk along the road or on a sidewalk. You're somewhere where lots of people live.
你会沿路边或人行道走，周围有很多人居住。

5
00:00:25,481 --> 00:00:30,400
When you hike, when you go for a hike though, it usually means you're somewhere like this.
而说到徒步，通常是指来到这样的地方。

6
00:00:30,400 --> 00:00:39,241
You're somewhere out in nature where you can enjoy the sunshine, the trees and just getting away from the busyness of city life or town life.
你在大自然中，能享受阳光和树木，暂时远离城市生活的忙碌。

7
00:00:39,241 --> 00:00:47,161
Now when you go for a hike you don't just go into the woods and start walking. You usually look for a trail.
徒步通常不是随意走进树林，而是先找到一条小径。

8
00:00:47,161 --> 00:00:56,081
Usually there is a path or trail. We use both words in English, and you can walk down that trail when you go for your hike.
通常会有一条路或小径，英语里 path 和 trail 都会用到，你可以沿着它走。

9
00:00:56,081 --> 00:01:01,481
This is a very well maintained trail. It's very, very nice, nice to walk on this trail.
这条小径维护得很好，走起来很舒服。

10
00:01:01,481 --> 00:01:08,041
And there's a nice sign here that tells us about this trail. It's called the Lookout Trail and it's about a kilometer long.
这里有块介绍小径的标牌，这条路线叫 Lookout Trail，长约一公里。

11
00:01:08,041 --> 00:01:14,841
It's just under a kilometer in length, and it should take about 25 minutes to walk this trail.
准确说还不到一公里，走完大约要二十五分钟。

12
00:01:14,841 --> 00:01:21,720
So once again when you go for a hike, you don't just walk into the woods willy nilly. Do you know that word?
再说一遍，徒步时不要随意闯进树林。你认识 willy nilly 这个说法吗？

13
00:01:21,720 --> 00:01:28,841
You look for trails and you stay on the trails. It's important to stay on the trails. I'll tell you why in just a moment.
要找小径，并沿着小径走。为什么这样很重要，马上会说到。

14
00:01:28,841 --> 00:01:32,521
It's important to stay on the trails for a couple of reasons.
沿着小径走有几个原因。

15
00:01:32,521 --> 00:01:40,201
The first reason is that there are some plants in this part of Ontario, Canada, that aren't very good for you.
第一个原因是加拿大安大略这一带有些植物会让人不舒服。

16
00:01:40,201 --> 00:01:43,521
There's something in particular called poison ivy.
其中有一种叫 poison ivy，也就是毒葛。

17
00:01:43,521 --> 00:01:54,440
If you go off the path, so as we look here at the path, if you were to go off the path eventually you might walk through some poison ivy.
如果离开小径，就像这里这样走进去，可能会经过一片毒葛。

18
00:01:54,440 --> 00:01:58,161
And then you will be very itchy for a number of days.
接触之后可能会痒上好几天。

19
00:01:58,161 --> 00:02:07,721
Poison ivy is not a nice thing to have touch your skin, so if you're wearing shorts for sure don't ever go off the path.
老师说，毒葛接触皮肤会不舒服，所以穿短裤时更不该离开小径。

20
00:02:07,721 --> 00:02:11,641
The other thing is that you might encounter dangerous animals.
另一个原因是可能遇到危险的动物。

21
00:02:11,641 --> 00:02:22,841
There aren't many dangerous animals here, but in northern Onario and in other parts of Canada, if you're out for a hike it's very important that you stick to the paths and trails.
这里危险动物不多，但在安大略北部和加拿大其他地方徒步时，沿小径走很重要。

22
00:02:22,841 --> 00:02:28,721
Because if you don't, you might encounter something like a bear or another dangerous animal.
因为偏离小径，可能会遇到熊等危险动物。

23
00:02:28,721 --> 00:02:33,841
And then the third reason is it just helps nature to stay beautiful.
第三个原因是这样有助于保护自然景观。

24
00:02:33,841 --> 00:02:42,561
If we were to all walk through the woods all the time, we would trample a lot of things that are growing there, and it wouldn't stay beautiful.
如果大家都随意穿过树林，就会踩坏许多生长中的植物，自然也不再那么美。

25
00:02:42,561 --> 00:02:53,520
So the best way to enjoy nature is to stay on the paths and trails when you go on a hike and just appreciate the stuff that you're seeing.
所以，老师建议沿着路径徒步，好好欣赏眼前的景色。

26
00:02:53,520 --> 00:02:59,761
One of the coolest things about going on a hike is sometimes you're able to see wildlife.
徒步很棒的一点是，有时能看到野生动物。

27
00:02:59,761 --> 00:03:06,160
Now I talked about wildlife that is dangerous, but some wildlife is not dangerous at all.
刚才提到危险的野生动物，不过也有些并不危险。

28
00:03:06,160 --> 00:03:15,681
This is a squirrel. This is probably the most common animal that you will see if you go on a hike in Ontario, Canada.
这是一只松鼠。在安大略徒步时，这大概是最常见的动物。

29
00:03:15,681 --> 00:03:23,201
You'll also see lots of birds. Um, you'll see chipmunks. You might see a raccoon. You might even see a skunk.
还会看见很多鸟、花栗鼠，也可能遇到浣熊，甚至臭鼬。

30
00:03:23,201 --> 00:03:27,880
By the way, if you see a skunk, you should go the other direction.
顺便说一句，老师提醒遇见臭鼬时往相反方向走。

31
00:03:27,880 --> 00:03:35,121
But one of the cool fun things about going for a hike is there's a good chance that you'll see some wildlife.
总之，徒步一个有趣的地方是，很有机会看见野生动物。

32
00:03:35,121 --> 00:03:44,761
Now if you're just out for a quick hike like I am, you don't need any special gear. I'm just wearing normal running shoes.
如果只是像我这样短途走走，就不用特别装备，我只穿了普通跑鞋。

33
00:03:44,761 --> 00:03:50,201
It's good to have appropriate footwear on when you go for a hike.
徒步时，穿合适的鞋很重要。

34
00:03:50,201 --> 00:03:59,991
But if you were more serious and if you were going for a longer hike, you might buy hiking boots. You might have walking sticks.
如果计划走更长、更正式的路线，可能会准备徒步靴和登山杖。

35
00:04:00,001 --> 00:04:06,561
You might bring a backpack with lots of supplies, like some food that you can eat for your hike.
也可能背一个装着补给的包，比如路上吃的食物。

36
00:04:06,561 --> 00:04:11,160
But I'm just out here for a simple hike. I'm not going for very long.
不过我只是来简单走一走，不会走很久。

37
00:04:11,160 --> 00:04:15,681
I'm going for about as long as it takes to make this English lesson.
大概就走到这节英语课拍完。

38
00:04:15,681 --> 00:04:21,280
So all I need is a nice pair of shoes and a sweatshirt, and I'm good to go.
所以，一双合适的鞋、一件卫衣，我就准备好了。
